  "extraction_notes": "The catalyst DATB 8a is not drawn; it is likely di(2,4,6-triisopropylphenyl)borinic acid or a related borinic acid based on the literature context, but is recorded here only by name as it's not explicitly drawn in the figure. Amine 11a was interpreted as 4-fluorophenethylamine in both 21 and 25 based on the kinking of the ethyl chain, despite the slightly different drawings. Reaction 22 was noted as 'gram scale'. Reactions 17-28 are examples of the general amidation scheme."
